course: dictionary
lesson: 1455
title: Who takes your money?
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A cashier is the person who takes your money when you buy something in a shop, bank or café, and gives you back any change. The word cash means money, so a cashier works with cash.
explain: The context shows what cashiers do. «If you get too much change, you tell the cashier and give it back, because that is honest.» The cashier is the person you talk to at the checkout, where you pay.
explain: «A boy in Chicago is given a dollar too much in change; he says, "I think you gave me too much," and the cashier thanks him.» To check the meaning, swap in "the person who takes payment". If the sentence still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: A cashier is a person who takes payment and gives change in a shop, bank or café.
fact: The till, also called the cash register, is the machine where the cashier keeps the money.
fact: When you pay at the checkout, you pay the cashier.
fact: «Cashiers» is the plural, so a big supermarket may have many cashiers.
fact: «Pay the cashier» and «at the checkout» are phrases you will hear in shops.
exercise: «If you get too much change, you tell the cashier and give it back.» Who is the cashier? | The shop's delivery driver | The person who sweeps the floor | The customer who is buying the shopping | *The person who takes payment and gives change
exercise: Which word means the machine where the money is kept? | receipt | customer | *till | cashier
exercise: Mia pays at the checkout and the cashier gives her change. What does Mia get back? | A new cashier | A bus ticket | *Money left over after paying | A bag of shopping
test: «A boy in Chicago is given a dollar too much; the cashier thanks him.» Why does the cashier thank the boy? | He paid with a card | *He was honest and told her she had given him too much change | He asked for a bag | He was rude to her
test: What is a cashier's main job? | *To take payment and give change | To stock the shelves | To drive the delivery van | To sweep the floor
exam: Where would you pay the cashier? | In the park on the swings | At the bus stop, waiting for a bus | Inside your bedroom | *At the checkout in a supermarket
